| `tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.network` | string | `none` for `unit`; `loopback` for `integration` and `e2e`; `any` for `smoke` | a tier marker name mapped to `none`, `loopback` or `any`: a closed set | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`load_policy`), installed by `tests/conftest.py` | Sets where a test whose closest tier marker is `<tier>` may connect or send: `none` refuses every socket connect, sendto and sendmsg with an address except to an AF_UNIX path under a temp root, `loopback` also allows 127.0.0.0/8, `::1` and the name `localhost`, and `any` allows every address. A reach outside it fails the test, named, even when the test catches the error. A test with no marker this block names gets `none`. An unknown value, a tier missing an axis, or `tests.isolation.tiers` absent stops pytest before any test runs (exit 4). | a name lookup, which the guard does not judge by choice because the connect that follows is judged, or a child process's connection, which no audit event carries | always |
